  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PESRTD land inventory in Burkina Faso 2017-2021 - Land inventory in Burkina Faso PESRTD</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PESRTD markinventering i Burkina Faso 2017-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Jorderosionen minskar Burkina Fasos jordbrukspotential och landets regering &#xe4;mnar utarbeta en strategi och en arbetsplan f&#xf6;r att v&#xe4;nda den negativa trenden. Som underlag f&#xf6;r dessa kr&#xe4;vs en inventering av marktillst&#xe5;ndet i landet. Insatsen syftar till att finansiera denna inventering inkl f&#xf6;rslag p&#xe5; handlingsprogram. Arbetet samordnas av milj&#xf6;ministeriet och i det deltar &#xe4;ven jordbruksministeriet och andra myndigheter. Insatsen har en budget om 500 000 kr f&#xf6;r fas 1 men genom avtalstill&#xe4;gg nr 3 &#xf6;kades denna till 1 573 000 kr samtidigt som aktivitetsperioden f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngdes till 20211031 och avtalets giltighet till 20220522.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Soil erosion is reducing the agricultural potential in Burkina faso and the country&apos;s government will therefore formulate a strategy and a work plan for reversing the negative trend. As a basis for these, a national inventory of the soil condition is necessary. The contribution aims at funding such an inventory and the formulation of a draft work plan. This work will be coordinated by the Ministry of Environment and carried out in collaboration with the Ministry of Agriculture and other governemental actors. The contribution had initially a budget of 500 000 SEK but it was increased to 1 573 000 kr with the agreement amendment no 3 and the activity period extended to 20211031 as well as the agreement&apos;s validity to 20220531.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objectives of the intervention are:

- evaluate the degradation trends in each geographical region of the country;

- determine the degradation hotspots for each region and propose neutrality indicators as well as measures to attain these;

- validate the generated information for each region and prepare an action plan for each region as well as for the whole country;

- integrate the generated information into national and regional policies and programs, including the Programme National du Secteur Rural (PNSR3);

- identify transformative projects/programs and innovative financing mechanisms for achieving soil neutrality in Burkina Faso.</narrative>
  </description>
